# No agent attribution in commits or PRs

Commit messages, PR titles and PR bodies must not mention Cursor, the agent or AI. Forbidden, for example:

- `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>` (or any `Co-authored-by` for an AI)
- `Made with Cursor`, `Generated by ...`, `Signed-off-by` for an AI, links to cursor.com

Author and committer stay the repo's `git config user.name` / `user.email`; never pass `--author` or set another identity.

Use skill `no-cursor-attribution` (`.cursor/skills/no-cursor-attribution/` or `~/.cursor/skills/no-cursor-attribution/`).

## After every `git commit`

Cursor appends the trailer to every agent `git commit`, also to `git commit --amend`, so amending does not help. Prefer the skill script (handles merge parents):

```bash
bash .cursor/skills/no-cursor-attribution/scripts/strip-commit-attribution.sh
# or: bash ~/.cursor/skills/no-cursor-attribution/scripts/strip-commit-attribution.sh
```

Inline equivalent (single-parent commits):

```bash
git log -1 --format=%B | grep -Eiv '^(co-authored-by|signed-off-by):.*(cursor|\bagent\b|\bai\b)|made with cursor|cursoragent@cursor\.com' \
  | git stripspace > /tmp/commit-msg \
  && NEW=$(git commit-tree "HEAD^{tree}" -p HEAD~1 -F /tmp/commit-msg) \
  && git diff --quiet HEAD "$NEW" \
  && git update-ref "refs/heads/$(git branch --show-current)" "$NEW" HEAD \
  && git log -1 --format=%B   # must show no attribution
```

- For a merge commit, pass every parent (`-p HEAD^1 -p HEAD^2`), or use the script.
- If the trailer is still there, stop and tell the user (permanent fix: Cursor Settings > Agent > Attribution, or Git & PRs > Attribution from Cursor 3.11, turn off).
- Only rewrite commits that are not pushed yet. For pushed commits, ask the user before rewriting history or force-pushing.

## PRs

Write the PR body yourself with `gh pr create --title ... --body-file <file>`; strip before create and verify afterwards:

```bash
bash .cursor/skills/no-cursor-attribution/scripts/strip-pr-attribution.sh --in-place /tmp/pr-body.md
gh pr view --json body -q .body
```
